      "message": "FYI, we had this deployed internally and ran into rewinds which we believe were due to the potential premature unlock fixed in https://review.gerrithub.io/c/eclipse-jgit/jgit/+/1245200. When the first repack is skipped, it creates a much higher chance that the premature unlock will happen, thus exposing the race more.\n\nThe premature unlock only happens when the second repack actually has a reason to delete the loose ref (and inadvertently also its lock). This could only happen if a loose ref were created after the first repack, which is a pretty small race window normally. However, when this change skips the first repack, it can cause the inadvertent unlock to happen anytime a ref was loose before entering this transaction, which on our one server is almost always.",
